      instead of a published figure. */}
  <section class="pc-fit" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <div class="pc-fit__inner">
      <div class="pc-fit__columns">
        <div class="pc-fit__col">
          <h3 class="ac-type-h3-home-route">Usually a fit</h3>
          <ul class="pc-check-list">
            {goodFit.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="pc-fit__aside">
            If this is a family or estate matter rather than a landlord or owner turnover,
            <a href="/estate-cleanout-san-jose/"> estate cleanout</a> is usually the closer match.
            If the property's main issue is heavy accumulation rather than a transition,
            <a href="/hoarding-cleanup-san-jose/"> hoarding cleanup</a> covers that.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pc-fit__col pc-fit__col--out">
          <h3 class="ac-type-h3-home-route">Probably not a fit</h3>
          <ul class="pc-minus-list">
            {poorFit.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="pc-fit__aside">
            If a junk hauler is genuinely all the property needs, use one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-price">
        <div class="pc-price__copy">
          <h3 class="ac-type-h3-home-feature">We price the property we see.</h3>
          <p>
            A one-bedroom unit and a four-bedroom house with a packed garage are not the same
            job, and a published starting figure would only ever be honest about one of them.
            Larger cleanouts usually need photographs and often a walkthrough before a firm scope
            and price.
          </p>
          <p class="pc-price__fee">{site.offer.assessmentFraming(site.offer.assessmentFee)}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pc-price__drivers">
          <p class="pc-price__label">What moves the number</p>
          <ul class="pc-rule-list pc-rule-list--tight">
            {priceDrivers.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ══ 08 · QUESTIONS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      Open Q&A, not an accordion — same reasoning as Hoarding and Estate. */}
  <section class="pc-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
